say something real quick. So this is my opinion, and I'm not saying that this is necessarily correct. But I think that people who watch films at home have no respect for film. And I know that sounds harsh, but I think it's true. Like if you're watching a movie on your phone or even on a TV, you're not really experiencing film. It's like you're consuming media. That's all. And then they say, oh, well, I watched a great movie last night. Yeah? Well, maybe you did. But you didn't experience film. Because film is not just a story. It's a medium. It's a craft. It's a whole art form. And if you don't go to the theater, you're missing the point. The way the filmmaker intended it to be seen. And that's why I think people who watch movies at home have no respect for film.

